{"text": "Canyon Rim Pediatrics, P.A. - Office visit\n\nPatient\tDOB\tMRN\tVisit date\n\nOKAFOR-JIMENEZ, MATEO\t04/17/2019\tCRP-0088214\t10/27/2026\n\nProvider: Hannah Goldfarb-Reyes, MD (NPI 1629407715). Accompanied by: mother, Adaeze Okafor. Insurance: Sandia Peaks Health Cooperative, member ID SPH-771-204-88-02.\n\nSubjective\n\nMateo is a 7-year-old boy with type 1 diabetes (diagnosed March 2024) and mild persistent asthma, here for a three-month follow-up. Mom reports two overnight lows in the 50s in the past month, both after soccer. No ketones, no ER visits. He used his rescue inhaler about twice a week during the smoke days in September.\n\nSchool: second grade at Juniper Ridge Elementary. The school nurse, Tamsin Whitehorse, has asked for an updated diabetes plan; his 504 plan is due for review. Mom says Ms. Whitehorse is only on site Mondays and Wednesdays.\n\nSocial: Parents separated in the spring. Mateo is with his father, Luis Jimenez, on alternate weekends. Mom is worried that dad does not count carbs and that weekend numbers run high. She asked that the pump reports not be mailed to the old address. Family speaks Igbo and Spanish at home; Mateo answers me in English.\n\nObjective\n\nMeasure\tToday\tLast visit\n\nWeight\t24.1 kg\t23.2 kg\n\nHeight\t124 cm\t122.5 cm\n\nA1c\t7.9%\t7.4%\n\nTime in range\t58%\t66%\n\nExam: well appearing, lungs clear, mild lipohypertrophy at the left abdomen infusion sites. Insulin pump serial PAA-3381-20417; CGM transmitter 8HX2K7, paired to mom's phone.\n\nAssessment and plan\n\n- Type 1 diabetes, above goal (ICD-10 E10.65). Change overnight basal from 0.35 units/hr to 0.30 units/hr on activity days. Rotate sites; avoid left abdomen for a month.\n\n- Asthma, controlled (J45.30). Continue fluticasone 44 mcg, 2 puffs twice daily. Flu vaccine given today, lot UJ417AB.\n\n- Refills sent to Mesa Vista Pharmacy, 505-555-0112: insulin lispro, Rx #7740291; test strips.\n\n- New school orders faxed to the nurse at 505-555-0191. Copy to mom through the portal, https://portal.canyonrimpeds.example/chart/0088214.\n\n- Offered a visit with our social worker about the two-household routine. Mom will think about it. With her consent I will send Mr. Jimenez the same carb-counting handout; his email on file is luis.jimenez77@inbox.example.\n\nBilling: CPT 99214. Return in 3 months, sooner for lows under 54.\n\nSigned electronically, H. Goldfarb-Reyes MD, 10/27/2026 4:52 PM", "kind": "Web page", "detail": "368 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Mateo", "Adaeze Okafor", "Hannah Goldfarb-Reyes", "Tamsin Whitehorse", "Luis Jimenez", "Ms. Whitehorse", "Mom", "Mr. Jimenez", "H. Goldfarb-Reyes"], "companies": ["Canyon Rim Pediatrics, P.A.", "Sandia Peaks Health Cooperative", "Juniper Ridge Elementary", "Mesa Vista Pharmacy"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Canyon Rim Pediatrics, P.A.", "Juniper Ridge Elementary", "Mesa Vista Pharmacy"], "health": ["diabetes", "type 1 diabetes", "asthma", "overnight lows", "resuce inhaler", "fluticasone", "insulin", "insulin lispro", "test strips", "CPT 99214", "lows"], "sensitive": ["parents separated", "father"], "names": ["Mateo", "Hannah Goldfarb-Reyes", "Adaeze", "Luis", "Tamsin", "H. Goldfarb-Reyes"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.7000000029802322, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "street", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "region", "names", "sensitive_topics"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 27, "text": "Canyon Rim Pediatrics, P.A.", "kind": "company", "source": "model", "canonical": "Canyon Rim Pediatrics, P.A."}, {"start": 72, "end": 93, "text": "OKAFOR-JIMENEZ, MATEO", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", 